            <ArticleTitle>Electrophysiological approaches to the study of bradykinin and nitric oxide in inflammatory pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>358-65</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>These electrophysiological studies, using desensitization and selective antagonists, demonstrate a peripheral role of bradykinin in the generation of pain in the rat. In addition, nitric oxide is shown to play a complex role in peripheral and spinal events in nociception.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
